    "ioctl_note": "RM requests computed as _IOWR(NV_IOCTL_MAGIC, escape, struct) following the __NV_IOWR macro in kernel-open/common/inc/nv.h (cited, not included: nv.h drags kernel-only definitions); UVM requests are the raw numbers (UVM_IOCTL_BASE(i) == i on Linux).",
    "nvtypes_note": "Two nvtypes.h exist. gcc -H: src/common/sdk/nvidia/inc/nvtypes.h (da23dbc2) is included first and defines NVTYPES_INCLUDED; kernel-open/common/inc/nvtypes.h (878e5711) is opened later via nv_uvm_user_types.h and its body is skipped by the identical guard. Their textual diff is limited to _MSC_VER/NV_WINDOWS blocks, so the Linux/gcc type widths are the same.",
    "pte_kind_note": "NV_MMU_PTE_KIND_* from the published Turing header turing/tu102/dev_mmu.h (GENERIC_MEMORY 0x06; hopper/gh100 repeats 0x6; ampere/ga100 only adds kinds). No ada/ad102 dev_mmu.h is published in this export: applying the Turing/Ampere kind table to AD102 is a PROFILE assumption recorded in SOURCE_LEDGER L-A19.",
    "source": "abi/abi_probe.c"
  },
